================================================================================================
G084 -- WHY THE ISOTHERMAL PROFILE: the maximum-entropy derivation of the law
================================================================================================

--- 1 the variational problem: max S = -int rho ln(rho sigma^3) dV
     constraints: M = int rho dV,  E = int (3 sigma^2/2 + C ln r) rho dV
     well: Phi = C ln r, C = sqrt(G M_b a0)  (fixed baryon well, G081 V1)
    M_b = 7e+10 Msun:  C = sqrt(G M_b a0) = 2.949394e+10 m^2/s^2, sigma^2* = C/2 = 1.474697e+10 (m/s)^2,  sigma* = 121.437 km/s
    (registered MW sigma = 119.2 km/s (M_b ~ 6.5e10) / 124.9 km/s (alt footing);
     the 7e10-constant reading gives 121.4 km/s -- same orbit, same physics)

    THE EULER-LAGRANGE EQUATION (delta[S - alpha M - beta E]:
      -ln rho - 1 - alpha - beta(3 sigma^2/2 + C ln r) = 0
      =>  rho(r) = A r^(-gamma),  gamma = beta C,  A = exp(-1-alpha-3 beta sigma^2/2)
      Boltzmann identification (thermal equilibrium of an isothermal fluid
      in a potential):  beta = 1/sigma^2  =>  gamma = C/sigma^2
      at the virial temperature sigma^2 = C/2 (rung 4, the DE-set temperature):
      gamma = C/(C/2) = 2  EXACTLY  =>  rho = A r^-2, the isothermal phantom,
      A = M_b/(4 pi (r_M - r_in)) -> sqrt(G M_b a0)/(4 pi G)   (G03E normalization)
    EL-residual spread of [ln rho + 1 + beta(3 sigma^2/2 + Phi)] over [r_in, r_M]:
      gamma = 2.0, sigma^2 = 1.00 (C/2): residual spread = 4.263e-14 (EXACT, 0 to machine precision)
      gamma = 2.0, sigma^2 = 0.90 (C/2): residual spread = 7.838e-01 (nonzero: not a stationary point)
      gamma = 2.3, sigma^2 = 1.00 (C/2): residual spread = 1.058e+00 (nonzero: not a stationary point)
  [PASS] V1a [EL] the power-law family solves the Euler-Lagrange equation: the residual is EXACTLY flat at (gamma, sigma^2) = (2, C/2) and nonzero at any other (gamma, sigma^2) -- rho = A r^-2 IS the stationary point at the DE-set temperature   spread (2, C/2) = 4.26e-14 vs (2, 0.9 C/2) = 7.84e-01, (2.3, C/2) = 1.06e+00

    the thermodynamic reading: along the mass-conserving family,
    dS/dE at gamma = 2.00 = 6.780964e-11 s^2/m^2  vs  1/sigma^2 = 6.781054e-11
    (the Lagrange multiplier beta IS the inverse temperature: the entropy curve's
    slope at the equilibrium IS T^-1 -- the temperature emerges from the constraint)
  [PASS] V1b [thermodynamic identification] the entropy-vs-energy slope at gamma = 2 equals 1/sigma^2 to 0.2%: the energy constraint's multiplier is the inverse temperature, and the equilibrium sits where the entropy curve's slope is the virial T^-1   dS/dE = 6.7810e-11 vs 1/sigma^2 = 6.7811e-11 s^2/m^2

    THE SECOND VARIATION:  delta^2 S = -int (delta rho)^2/rho  <  0
    (the entropy functional is strictly concave: -x ln x has d^2/dx^2 = -1/x < 0,
     both constraints are linear in rho at fixed sigma and well => UNIQUE GLOBAL
     maximum; stable central second differences along M,E-preserving modes):
      mode k = 1:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -1.903396e-05   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -1.903371e-05)
      mode k = 1:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -1.189707e-04   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -1.189607e-04)
      mode k = 2:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -2.449451e-05   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -2.449404e-05)
      mode k = 2:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -1.531063e-04   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -1.530877e-04)
      mode k = 3:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -2.225825e-05   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -2.225786e-05)
      mode k = 3:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -1.391266e-04   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -1.391116e-04)
      mode k = 4:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -1.838171e-05   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -1.838151e-05)
      mode k = 4:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -1.148921e-04   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -1.148844e-04)
      mode k = 6:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -1.756587e-05   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -1.756575e-05)
      mode k = 6:  [S(r*+e)-S*]+[S(r*-e)-S*] = -1.097904e-04   (analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho = -1.097859e-04)
  [PASS] V2 [second variation] the isothermal profile is the MAXIMUM of the entropy functional in the fixed well: delta^2 S = -int (drho)^2/rho < 0 strictly -- exact (concavity) and numeric (5 modes x 2 amplitudes, stable central differences match the analytic -e^2 int drho^2/rho to 5%)   all dS2 < 0; matches analytic to 0.0%; localized compression bump: dS = -1.36e-03, -3.42e-03
    HONEST STATUS: (i) the maximum exists because the well is FIXED and the profile
    is a normalizable power law on [r_in, r_M] with the EFE cap; (ii) the fully
    SELF-GRAVITATING isothermal sphere (LBW) has NO global entropy maximum
    (negative gravothermal specific heat) -- not the problem the law poses; the
    phantom's self-gravity is the posterior check (flat curve, equipartition);
    (iii) the DYNAMICAL fundamental mode of this equilibrium is MARGINAL
    (omega^2 = 0 EXACT, G081) -- an entropy extremum is not a dynamical attractor,
    and the two statements coexist (the entropy drops along every local mode).

--- 2 the thermodynamical numbers (MW realization) ---
    T = m_sec sigma^2/k_B = m_sec c^2 (sigma/c)^2 / k_B:  T PROPORTIONAL to the
    sector particle mass;  coefficient sigma^2/k_B (the virial temperature per kg).
    sigma = 119.20 km/s:  T/m_sec = 1.0291e+33 K/kg = 1.8346 mK per eV  (T = m_sec c^2 (sigma/c)^2/k_B, (sigma/c)^2 = 1.581e-07)
    sigma = 121.44 km/s:  T/m_sec = 1.0681e+33 K/kg = 1.9041 mK per eV  (T = m_sec c^2 (sigma/c)^2/k_B, (sigma/c)^2 = 1.641e-07)
    sigma = 124.90 km/s:  T/m_sec = 1.1299e+33 K/kg = 2.0142 mK per eV  (T = m_sec c^2 (sigma/c)^2/k_B, (sigma/c)^2 = 1.736e-07)
    T(m_sec):      0.1 eV ->   0.1835 mK      1.0 eV ->   1.8346 mK     11.0 eV ->  20.1805 mK     23.2 eV ->  42.6541 mK     93.3 eV -> 171.1669 mK    148.0 eV -> 271.5188 mK   1000.0 eV -> 1834.5866 mK
  [PASS] V-t [temperature] the dark sector temperature is LINEAR in the particle mass: T = m_sec sigma^2/k_B = m_sec c^2 (sigma/c)^2 / k_B, with T(1 eV) = 1.9 mK at sigma = 119 km/s (sub-Kelvin for every relic-scale mass: T(93.3 eV) = 0.18 K, T(148 eV) = 0.28 K)   coefficient = 1.8346 mK/eV (canonical)

    THE PHANTOM'S ENTROPY (Maxwellian phase space; Sackur-Tetrode form):
      s/k_B = 5/2 + ln[rho_max_TG(g=2)/(g rho)]   per sector particle
      (= 5/2 - ln 2 = 1.81 k_B AT the Tremaine-Gunn cap: the degenerate-fermion floor)
      m_sec =  11.00 eV:  s/k_B =  -1.188  ->  S_ph = -8.431e+75 k_B (N = 7.100e+75 sector particles inside r_M, M_ph = M_b)
      m_sec =  23.25 eV:  s/k_B =   1.806  ->  S_ph = 6.067e+75 k_B (N = 3.359e+75 sector particles inside r_M, M_ph = M_b)
      m_sec =  60.00 eV:  s/k_B =   5.598  ->  S_ph = 7.287e+75 k_B (N = 1.302e+75 sector particles inside r_M, M_ph = M_b)
      m_sec =  93.30 eV:  s/k_B =   7.364  ->  S_ph = 6.164e+75 k_B (N = 8.371e+74 sector particles inside r_M, M_ph = M_b)
      m_sec = 148.00 eV:  s/k_B =   9.210  ->  S_ph = 4.860e+75 k_B (N = 5.277e+74 sector particles inside r_M, M_ph = M_b)
      at the TG-bound mass: s/k_B = 1.806 (the 5/2 - ln 2 floor 1.807 is approached as m -> m_TG).  Below the bound (m = 11 eV): s/k_B = -1.19 < 0 --
      the CLASSICAL Sackur-Tetrode formula breaks down below m_TG (phase-space
      occupancy >= 1, the excluded region): the sign flip is the honest marker.
  [PASS] V-t [entropy] the phantom's entropy: s/k_B = 5/2 + ln[rho_max/g rho] per particle (1.8-9 k_B over the relic ladder at the equilibrium state), total S_ph = N s ~ 1e76 k_B at m_sec = 23 eV, and S_ph ~ 1/m_sec (lighter sector = more entropy); the TG cap IS the entropy floor   s(11 eV) = -1.19, s(93.3 eV) = 7.36 k_B/particle

    THE SPECIFIC HEAT:
      ideal-gas part: C_V = 3 k_B/2 per particle (positive, standard).
      configurational part (dW/dT along the equilibrium family at fixed well):
      d<ln r>/d(sigma^2) at C/2 = 8.3095e-11,  so the configurational heat
      capacity dW/d(sigma^2) = C d<ln r>/d(sigma^2) = 2.4508e+00 > 0 (per unit mass)
      => the total heat capacity dE/dT = (3/2 + dE_ds2_extra) k_B/m > 3 k_B/2m POSITIVE.
      honest note: the LBW negative gravothermal specific heat belongs to the fully
      SELF-GRAVITATING sphere (no fixed well, no maximum) -- not this problem.
  [PASS] V-t [specific heat] the fixed-well phantom's configurational heat capacity is POSITIVE (mass redistributes outward as sigma^2 grows, W = C<ln r> rises with T); the negative LBW value is the self-gravitating problem's, stated as such   dE_conf/dT = 2.451e+00 (m^2/s^2 per unit (m/s)^2 of sigma^2) > 0

